cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Automated pollinator detection for rare California coastal
  plants: a YOLOv8 pipeline for camera-trap footage
message: >-
  If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it using
  the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Katerina
    family-names: Bischel
    affiliation: >-
      Cheadle Center for Biodiversity and Ecological Restoration,
      University of California, Santa Barbara
abstract: >-
  A YOLOv8-based detection pipeline for identifying bumblebee
  visitors to two federally endangered California coastal plant
  species, Ventura marsh milk-vetch (Astragalus pycnostachyus var.
  lanosissimus) and salt marsh bird's-beak (Chloropyron maritimum
  ssp. maritimum), from camera-trap video recorded at the North
  Campus Open Space restoration site in Goleta, California during
  the 2025 field season. The repository covers frame extraction,
  manual annotation, model training, evaluation, and hybrid
  detection-and-tracking for visitation events.
keywords:
  - pollinator monitoring
  - object detection
  - YOLOv8
  - computer vision
  - ecological restoration
  - endangered species
  - Bombus
  - camera trap
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/katerinabischell/bee-monitoring-ml'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2025-08-22'
